    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-testdata-datasource",
        "uid": "trlxrdZVk"
      },
      "description": "**Adversarial case for sankey.** TestData `node_graph` with `nodes.type: random` deliberately introduces cycles — `generateRandomNodes` has a loop commented \"Add some random edges to create possible cycle\".\n\nECharts' sankey layout throws `'Sankey is a DAG, the original data has cycle!'` on cyclic input, and that throw is **not** behind a `__DEV__` guard, so it reaches production. Any sankey converter must break cycles before handing links to ECharts; this panel is the fixture that proves it. `graph` and `chord` accept cycles fine.\n\nNote `seed` only drives edge topology — per-node stats, `icon`, `noderadius` and `highlighted` use bare `Math.random()`, so this panel is not pixel-reproducible.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 18
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "grafana-testdata-datasource",
            "uid": "trlxrdZVk"
          },
          "nodes": {
            "count": 10,
            "seed": 1,
            "type": "random"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "scenarioId": "node_graph"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Random — contains cycles (sankey adversarial case)",
      "type": "nodeGraph"
    },
